PART 2 — TECHNOLOGY STACK RECOMMENDATION & DECISION

2.1  Recommended Stack: Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS SPA
Given your development environment (Termux on Android, GitHub Pages hosting, zero build step requirement), the recommended stack is a single self-contained HTML file implementing a hash-based Single-Page Application. This is the optimal choice for your constraints and is the same battle-tested approach as the reference build.

Why NOT React, Next.js or Astro at this stage
React requires a build step (npm run build) — impractical as primary Termux workflow
Next.js requires a Node.js server or Vercel — cannot deploy to GitHub Pages without a CI pipeline
Astro also needs a build step and npm ecosystem — adds friction for a solo developer in Termux
None of these provide SEO advantages over vanilla JS at V1 scale (under 50 page routes)
Migration to Astro is the correct move at Phase 5 (Month 12+) when content team scales

Why Vanilla SPA on GitHub Pages IS the right call
Zero build step — edit index.html in any text editor, git push, site is live in 90 seconds
GitHub Pages serves static files natively — free, reliable, global CDN available via Cloudflare
Full control over every byte of CSS and JS — no framework overhead, fastest possible load times
Single file deployment — entire site is one index.html plus a small set of standalone .html files
Python scripts handle content assembly — run perfectly in Termux with no extra installs
Hash-based routing (#bookmakers, #slots, #soccer) works on GitHub Pages with zero server config
Scales comfortably to 50+ page routes before any migration is needed

