PART 4 — GITHUB PAGES DEPLOYMENT GUIDE (TERMUX WORKFLOW)

4.1  Overview
GitHub Pages is a free static hosting service that serves files directly from your GitHub repository. Push to the main branch and your site updates automatically within 60-90 seconds. Combined with a custom .co.za domain and Cloudflare CDN, this gives you production-grade hosting at zero recurring cost (excluding the domain ~R150/year).

4.2  One-Time Setup
Step 1 — Install Tools in Termux
pkg update && pkg upgrade -y
pkg install git python openssh nodejs -y

Step 2 — Configure Git Identity
git config --global user.name "YourName"
git config --global user.email "you@email.com"

Step 3 — Generate SSH Key for GitHub Authentication
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "you@email.com"
# Press enter 3 times to accept defaults
cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
# Copy the output text
Paste the copied key into GitHub: Settings > SSH and GPG keys > New SSH Key.

Step 4 — Create GitHub Repository
Go to github.com > click the + button > New repository
Name it your brand name (e.g. betsaguide) — this will be in your URL
Set Visibility to Public (required for free GitHub Pages)
Leave all initialise options unticked — start with an empty repo
Click Create repository

Step 5 — Initialise Local Project and Push
mkdir ~/betsaguide && cd ~/betsaguide
git init
touch index.html .nojekyll
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin git@github.com:YourUsername/betsaguide.git
git push -u origin main

Step 6 — Enable GitHub Pages
In your GitHub repository, click Settings
In the left sidebar click Pages
Under Source: select Deploy from a branch
Set Branch to main and Folder to / (root)
Click Save
Wait 60-90 seconds. Site is live at: https://yourusername.github.io/betsaguide/

TIP:  Create an empty file called .nojekyll in your repo root. This prevents GitHub Pages from running Jekyll, which can cause issues with files or folders that start with an underscore.

Step 7 — Connect Your Custom .co.za Domain
In Cloudflare: add your domain, update nameservers at Domains.co.za to Cloudflare NS1/NS2
In Cloudflare DNS: add A records for root domain (@) pointing to GitHub Pages IPs: 185.199.108.153, 185.199.109.153, 185.199.110.153, 185.199.111.153
In Cloudflare DNS: add CNAME record — Name: www, Target: yourusername.github.io
In GitHub repo Settings > Pages > Custom Domain: enter yourbrand.co.za and Save
Wait for DNS propagation (up to 24 hours) then tick Enforce HTTPS

4.3  Daily Deployment Workflow (Three Commands)
Every time you update the site the process is the same three commands:

cd ~/betsaguide
git add . && git commit -m "Update: brief description of what changed"
git push
# Site is live in ~90 seconds. No build step. No server.

