build_standalone.py — Generating Extension Pages
Use this script to generate standalone .html pages (e.g. detailed bookmaker review pages) that share the same nav and CSS as the main SPA but have their own URL. Each page is pre-rendered HTML with no router needed.

# Usage:
python3 scripts/build_standalone.py


# What it does:
# 1. Reads shared head_inner (CSS + nav) from main SPA
# 2. Reads page content from src/pages/betway-review.py
# 3. Assembles complete standalone HTML file
# 4. Writes to standalone/betway-review.html
# 5. Runs node --check to validate JS syntax

Critical: Apostrophe Safety in Python Strings
When writing page content in Python strings that inject into JS template literals, apostrophes in contractions MUST be escaped with a backslash. An unescaped apostrophe will terminate the JS string and cause a blank page.

# WRONG — breaks JS string:
content = "South Africa's top bookmaker"


# CORRECT — escaped apostrophe:
content = "South Africa\'s top bookmaker"


# Auto-fix pattern (run after writing content):
import re
content = re.sub(r"(?<!\\)([a-zA-Z])'([a-zA-Z])", r"\1\\'\2", content)



