APPENDICES

Appendix A — SA Betting Terminology Glossary
Term
Definition
Spina Zonke
isiZulu for 'spin everything' — the SA colloquial term for online slot games. Coined by Hollywoodbets. High-volume SA search term.
Fafi / Fah-Fee
Traditional SA numbers game. 36 numbers each associated with a dream meaning (e.g. number 1 = old woman, number 11 = carriage). Players bet on numbers based on dreams or omens.
PSL
Premier Soccer League — now officially the Betway Premiership. South Africa's top professional football division. Primary SA soccer betting category.
NRGP
National Responsible Gambling Programme. SA's national gambling addiction support body. Toll-free helpline: 0800 006 008 (24/7). Must appear on every page.
POPIA
Protection of Personal Information Act 2013. SA's primary data privacy legislation. Equivalent to GDPR. Requires privacy policy and cookie consent.
FICA
Financial Intelligence Centre Act. Requires SA bookmakers to verify customer identity before allowing withdrawals (copy of SA ID + proof of address). Known as FICA verification.
NGB
National Gambling Board. SA federal gambling regulator. All legal bookmakers must hold an NGB-recognised provincial gambling licence.
Data-Free
SA mobile carrier feature allowing access to specific apps or websites without consuming the user's mobile data. Betway and Hollywoodbets offer data-free access. Major SA differentiator.
EFT
Electronic Funds Transfer. Primary SA bank payment method. Direct bank-to-bank transfer. Most popular SA deposit and withdrawal method.
Ozow
SA instant EFT payment provider (formerly Pay@). Allows real-time bank transfers without sharing card details. Popular at most SA bookmakers.
1Voucher
SA prepaid voucher system. Purchased at retail outlets (Checkers, Pick n Pay, Shoprite). Popular deposit method for unbanked or privacy-conscious SA bettors.
USSD
Unstructured Supplementary Service Data. Feature phone menu-based service (e.g. *120*xxx#). Hollywoodbets offers full USSD betting for users without smartphones or internet access.
Tote
Pari-mutuel pool betting system used in SA horse racing. Odds are determined by the total pool divided among winners, not set by the bookmaker.
CPA
Cost Per Acquisition. Affiliate commission model: you earn a fixed amount (e.g. R400) for each new player who registers and makes a qualifying first deposit.
RevShare
Revenue Share. Affiliate commission model: you earn an ongoing percentage (e.g. 25%) of the bookmaker's net revenue from players you referred.
FTD
First Time Deposit. The metric most affiliate programmes use to trigger CPA payments. A player must register AND make a qualifying deposit before you earn commission.
Punters Challenge
Hollywoodbets free weekly horse racing competition. Players predict race outcomes for a chance to win prizes. High engagement feature unique to Hollywoodbets.


